  "term": "cheating",
  "definition": "In educational settings, cheating is a form of academic misconduct in which a person uses dishonest or deceptive means to gain an unfair academic advantage. It can include exam cheating, using prohibited electronic devices or unauthorised materials, or obtaining access to questions in advance.",
